  "id": "day-03",
  "note": "The day the app says NOTHING, and the reason that is a fixture rather than an absence. A person who works in the one application they named, takes a break, pauses, walks away and gives a presentation has done nothing that warrants a word — and every gate that keeps the app quiet is exercised here in turn: the confident relevance that is the only thing buying silence under U-1, the session phase, the hardware idle source and the presentation gate. A guardian that could not produce a silent day would be a guardian nobody keeps installed, and this is the fixture that fails the moment one becomes impossible.",
